{"w": 595.3200073242188, "h": 809.0257568359375, "lines": [{"t": "47", "x": 0.904017983697097, "y": 0.9742087522985531, "w": 0.029725264906538765, "h": 0.017428414981790374, "c": 1, "size": 12.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "READING", "x": 0.39012631381883617, "y": 0.1569022641737755, "w": 0.13046254235434, "h": 0.023179739115831682, "c": 1, "size": 16.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "READING PASSAGE 1", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.21385968079554116, "w": 0.2852801181661608, "h": 0.023179739115831682, "c": 1, "size": 16.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1 - 13, which are based on Reading", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.24698839946471834, "w": 0.8261407720928716, "h": 0.01742835839970161, "c": 1, "size": 12.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "Passage 1 below.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.2731309842160114, "w": 0.15808640454521827, "h": 0.01742835839970161, "c": 1, "size": 12.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Manatees", "x": 0.4463649931415932, "y": 0.2993106113747501, "w": 0.15018475509300397, "h": 0.026142547029900542, "c": 1, "size": 18.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "Manatees, also known as sea cows, are aquatic mammals that belong to a group", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.3483918389616417, "w": 0.8260117957009852, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "of animals called Sirenia. This group also contains dugongs. Dugongs and", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.37672218903577936, "w": 0.8260115906510775, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "manatees look quite alike - they are similar in size, colour and shape, and both", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.40505257683130946, "w": 0.8262974302222854, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "have flexible flippers for forelimbs. However, the manatee has a broad, rounded", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.4333829646268396, "w": 0.8260337360410994, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "tail, whereas the dugong's is fluked, like that of a whale. There are three species", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.46171331470097726, "w": 0.8260771040965588, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "of manatees: The West Indian manatee (Trichechus manatus), the African", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.49006841000860196, "w": 0.8261725548285511, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "manatee (Trichechus senegalensis) and the Amazonian manatee (Trichechus", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5183987978041321, "w": 0.8260989419117193, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "inunguis).", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5467291478782698, "w": 0.10304588309510122, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Unlike most mammals, manatees have only six bones in their neck - most others,", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5750595356737999, "w": 0.8267464895199504, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "including humans and giraffes, have seven. This short neck allows a manatee to", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6033898857479375, "w": 0.8263442841261742, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "move its head up and down, but not side to side. To see something on its left or its", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6317203112648602, "w": 0.8262080284625676, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "right, a manatee must turn its entire body, steering with its flippers. Manatees", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6600877037464434, "w": 0.8257725024588047, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "have pectoral flippers but no back limbs, only a tail for propulsion. They do have", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6882698087480134, "w": 0.8264904847102998, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "pelvic bones, however - a leftover from their evolution from a four-legged to a", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.716600158822151, "w": 0.8266498084885125, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "fully aquatic animal. Manatees share some visual similarities to elephants. Like", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7449305088962886, "w": 0.825968325120572, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "elephants, manatees have thick, wrinkled skin. They also have some hairs covering", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7732608589704263, "w": 0.8266034672093928, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "their bodies which help them sense vibrations in the water around them.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8015912090445639, "w": 0.732690455736748, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Seagrasses and other marine plants make up most of a manatee's diet. Manatees", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8299216345614866, "w": 0.8262077208877061, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "spend about eight hours each day grazing and uprooting plants. They eat up to", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8582767298691113, "w": 0.8261206772019258, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "15% of their weight in food each day. African manatees are omnivorous - studies", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8866070799432489, "w": 0.8267505905181026, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}], "source": "pdf text layer"}